lf wt: add worktree management commands

Organize CLI into subcommands: `lf wt`, `lf pr`, `lf meta`. The new
`lf wt` commands manage git worktrees at `.lf/worktrees/`:

- `lf wt create <name>` - create worktree, branch, and open IDEs
- `lf wt open <name>` - reopen IDEs at existing worktree
- `lf wt list` - show worktrees with dirty/local status
- `lf wt clean` - remove worktrees for branches not on origin

IDE integration opens Warp and Cursor based on config settings. Falls
back to cursor alone if no workspace file found, or uses explicit
workspace path from config.

Moves `lf install`, `lf doctor`, `lf version` to `lf meta` namespace.
Moves `lf land` and PR creation to `lf pr` namespace. Top-level task
commands like `lf review` and pipelines remain unchanged.

Adds pydantic for validated config loading with IdeConfig model. Tests
updated to use PipelineConfig directly instead of Pipeline dataclass.
